    "media:imagetext": "AFRICA\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad.\nAfrica is a continent of great natural beauty. In addition to abundant wild game it contains a\nmixture of mountains, jungles, magnificent rivers, open plains, and arid deserts.\nMany of its cities are bustling metropolises with broad avenues, modern buildings.\ngood restaurants and fine hotels, including several Inter• Continental Hotels.\nFrom New York, Pan Am 747's serve Dakar, Monrovia, Acera, Lagos, Abidjan, and Nairobi.\nMr. Kingman's painting depicts majestic, snowcapped Mount Kilamanjaro in Tanzania\nAt 19,340 feet it is Africa's highest mountain\nOPAN AM",
